misc: hy310-motor: let probe skip homing

Probe arms a homing run, and homing starts by driving up to 100 msteps in one
direction. That is fine on a machine whose position is unknown but free -- and
wrong on one that is already parked against its end stop, which is exactly the
state this driver has to be able to diagnose. Loading the module to look at the
limiter then pushes the mechanism into the stop, once per load.

That happened here: with the focus driven to its upper end by hand, reloading
the module to read the limiter would have driven it further up, three times in
a row.

Add homing=0. The driver still probes, configures the pads and exposes sysfs;
it just does not move anything, and it says plainly that it has no calibration.
Default is unchanged.

    insmod hy310-focus-motor.ko homing=0 limiter_bias=1   # look, do not move

diff -ruN a/drivers/misc/hy310-focus-motor.c b/drivers/misc/hy310-focus-motor.c
--- a/drivers/misc/hy310-focus-motor.c	2026-09-07 20:33:31.054882654 +0200
+++ b/drivers/misc/hy310-focus-motor.c	2026-09-07 20:33:51.976259658 +0200
@@ -805,6 +805,20 @@
  * PH14 (stock_pinconf_pio.txt: "pin 238 (PH14): input bias pull down").
  */
 /*
+ * Probe arms a homing run, and homing starts by driving up to 100 msteps in
+ * one direction. If the mechanism is already parked against its end stop --
+ * which is exactly the state this driver has to be able to diagnose -- that
+ * run pushes into the stop. Loading the module merely to look at the limiter
+ * must therefore not move anything at all.
+ *
+ * With homing=0 the driver probes, configures the pads and exposes sysfs
+ * without touching the mechanism. It then has no calibration, and says so.
+ */
+static bool homing = true;
+module_param(homing, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(homing, "run the homing sequence at probe (default yes)");
+
+/*
  * Diagnostic override for the limiter pad bias. The switch on this board
  * sources 3.3 V when it is active and is open otherwise, so an open switch and
  * a broken connection look identical on a pull-down. A pull-up does not tell
@@ -1143,7 +1157,12 @@
 	g_motor = m;
 
 	/* Async homing — doesn't block probe, runs in work queue */
-	queue_delayed_work(m->wq, &m->homing_work, msecs_to_jiffies(500));
+	if (homing)
+		queue_delayed_work(m->wq, &m->homing_work,
+				   msecs_to_jiffies(500));
+	else
+		dev_warn(&pdev->dev,
+			 "homing disabled by module parameter — position unknown and uncalibrated\n");
 
 	dev_info(&pdev->dev, "probed: %d phases, %d limiters, %d steps\n",
 		 m->phase_num, m->limiter_num, m->step_total);
